{"event_type":"review","id":"435fbfed58293d6f303d57284c1303ea49518102a21ca068fedc7f92e6458086","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T22:40:31Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/de2a5a01f3099decf91de01a34fa40c6eec1dcd1c73d40a1ccb7961d1c21e518","sha256":"de2a5a01f3099decf91de01a34fa40c6eec1dcd1c73d40a1ccb7961d1c21e518"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c5d090c8d5106f5a50ecbeb2e019d61e60ecba19c9ceae16294c47b4a5ddc806","sha256":"c5d090c8d5106f5a50ecbeb2e019d61e60ecba19c9ceae16294c47b4a5ddc806"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b56a9afded0ebf210c14693fc9b98cc4d657d64bdbc4fd16c1f7e834c30a3f71","sha256":"b56a9afded0ebf210c14693fc9b98cc4d657d64bdbc4fd16c1f7e834c30a3f71"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1262bc1533b452f8929988016f0aac824365470a0f0c5c162d0f34dbad2b10cc","sha256":"1262bc1533b452f8929988016f0aac824365470a0f0c5c162d0f34dbad2b10cc"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ae6297f61c0414ab428f08b787bf003518dff206122d3d95618b37b7a19586dd","sha256":"ae6297f61c0414ab428f08b787bf003518dff206122d3d95618b37b7a19586dd"}],"attempt_id":"59002021e19ea6435f958a4573bb5b4f45675368a9763cbd0f03e8258098f625:0:1","base":"9f1770647757ec1eafcb583556fd0b7b25f77e59","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"2122a29912b37120b91a3646437decb60dc5c3a6","body":"**Make the dispatch trust test reach trust validation.**\n\nThe dispatch test at lines 98-104 passes the shared `candidate` to `merge.classifyPrs`. That candidate carries `headRefName`, `baseRefName`, and `state`, which the strict classify input schema rejects. The job can therefore fail at schema parsing before trust validation runs. The `not.toBe('ok')` and `not.toContain('evil')` assertions would still pass if the trust check were removed.\n\nBuild the dispatch input from a candidate without those three fields, as the schema test does at lines 573-574. Assert that this input parses against the classify schema. Then assert that the job fails with the config error for `config.trustedBots` and that its result does not contain `evil`.","id":"04654f40baca501c923ad9a557bdc6a0752ed6ea9da9def49b808653ea6c43c4","intervals":[[103,104]],"path":"test/ops/merge/trustClassify.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make the dispatch trust test reach trust validation."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"2122a29912b37120b91a3646437decb60dc5c3a6","body":"**Remove the `.replace()` call from the planner comparison so an un-normalized base fails the test.**\n\nThe `replace('refs/heads/main', 'main')` runs on the serialized planner output. The planner returns its `baseBranch` value in that output. If the planner received an un-normalized `refs/heads/main`, the serialized result would contain `\"baseBranch\":\"refs/heads/main\"`. The replace would rewrite that string to `\"baseBranch\":\"main\"`, and the comparison with the `main` control would pass. Removing the replace makes that case fail. The correct path does not contain `refs/heads/main`, so the replace does nothing there and the test still passes. Also assert the returned base directly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      ).replace('refs/heads/main', 'main');\n+      );\n     expect(await planned('refs/heads/main')).toBe(await planned('main'));\n+    expect(await planned('main')).toContain('\"baseBranch\":\"main\"');\n```\n\n</details>","id":"ba312755a8c3d5014eddd31504e1032773aba565adefe3f6636ab8aca9abf150","intervals":[[178,178]],"path":"test/ops/merge/trustClassify.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Remove the `.replace()` call from the planner comparison so an un-normalized base fails the test."}],"head":"b36f8ab0adae73ae6ca69d28cde92e4226ec479d","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"1d0dfc2cfdcd23ed04a4bbe4d61d1448cc28ee8b","intervals":[[1,292]],"path":"test/ops/merge/executeMerges.helpers.ts"},{"blob":"59295b8196e41eec510547b21d2083b68bc2178f","intervals":[[1,1036]],"path":"test/ops/merge/executeMerges.safeArgs.test.ts"},{"blob":"7b61e244b7f8fa3b044166374a2c102bce285bdc","intervals":[[1,424]],"path":"test/ops/merge/resolveConflict.helpers.ts"},{"blob":"1b57a651a7e83d45652ac3197a38230eba502aa4","intervals":[[1,252]],"path":"test/ops/merge/resolveConflict.op-failures.test.ts"},{"blob":"e792295b4875465362561eba7adfab422478db73","intervals":[[1,272]],"path":"test/ops/merge/resolveConflict.op-outcomes.test.ts"},{"blob":"30e51e64eda6909d561244f5d557966194a845b7","intervals":[[1,882]],"path":"test/ops/merge/resolveConflict.publicationGate.test.ts"},{"blob":"975a6900f82605e66740770e33d8417d15495b66","intervals":[[1,332]],"path":"test/ops/merge/runPrs.helpers.ts"},{"blob":"2122a29912b37120b91a3646437decb60dc5c3a6","intervals":[[1,652]],"path":"test/ops/merge/trustClassify.test.ts"}],"job_id":"59002021e19ea6435f958a4573bb5b4f45675368a9763cbd0f03e8258098f625:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"1d0dfc2cfdcd23ed04a4bbe4d61d1448cc28ee8b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"test/ops/merge/executeMerges.helpers.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"59295b8196e41eec510547b21d2083b68bc2178f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"test/ops/merge/executeMerges.safeArgs.test.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"7b61e244b7f8fa3b044166374a2c102bce285bdc","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"test/ops/merge/resolveConflict.helpers.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"1b57a651a7e83d